{"Retry count writes use snapshot value from earlier findMany, so overlapping cron requests can read same count and write same next value, losing failed attempts and allowing retries past cleanup point": 0.8807901740074158, "Retry cleanup branch is not limited to unscheduled SMS reminders, so a reminder with retryCount > 1 that gets successfully scheduled in overlapping run can be deleted in next cron pass even though Twilio still holds the future SMS": 0.9735326766967773, "Transient errors (Twilio API errors, network timeouts, internal scheduling errors) increment retryCount the same as permanent failures, causing temporary outages to permanently delete reminders after two failures": 0.9672620296478271, "When SMS sending is locked for a user or team, scheduleSMS() returns falsy without making a Twilio call but still increments retryCount, deleting pending reminders for temporarily locked accounts after two cron runs": 0.954129159450531, "If twilio.scheduleSMS() succeeds but the following Prisma update for scheduled:true or referenceId throws, the catch path increments deletion counter while Twilio scheduled message exists, causing orphaned messages and potential duplicate schedules": 0.9675635099411011}